      "note": [
        "Commenced a specific course at a folk high school within 1, 3, 5 years \r\n Only includes long-term courses of the type “special course”. Special courses can be run at different levels – from compulsory-school level to post-secondary level. All special courses are included, even those that are not post-secondary courses. \r\n The statistics in this survey are presented net. This means that each individual is counted the first time the individual has studied in a special course at a folk high school. \r\n Eligibility from upper secondary school  All upper secondary school graduates automatically have basic eligibility for an institute of higher vocational education. All graduates from preparatory programmes for post-secondary education automatically have basic eligibility for an institute of higher education. Graduates from vocational programmes can add subjects to obtain basic eligibility for an institute of higher education. \r\n Grade point average from upper secondary school Students who have studied in the International Baccalaureate programme do not obtain course grades on the same scale as students who have studied in other programmes, and are thus not included in the presentation according to grade points.  \r\n Level of educational attainment of the parent(s)  Information on the parents’ level of education is obtained from the Register on educational attainment of the population. Information of the parents’ level of education is obtained, if possible, when the pupil was 12 years old. If data is available for both parents, the parent with the highest level of education is selected. \r\n To prevent disclosure of information, random rounding off was applied in the tables.  Cell values 1 and 2 have been rounded off to either 0 or 3 with predetermined probabilities. This is why the study domains sometimes do not add up to the total."
